Since rangers get the Longbow as their Quest artifact, to me the
issue is *when* which is best not which is best for the whole game.

> With highly enchanted daggers, arrows and bow, and very good
> strength, it seems that daggers were just as fast to kill as the bow
> and arrows.

Daggers do not disappear when thrown.  The Longbow can create
its own arrows.  This makes them early game and late game
approaches.  Save those skill slots for post Quest!

> On the other hand, that was the first time I ever had blessed +7
> arrows, and I was surprised that I never lost even one. Does anyone
> know the chances of losing ammo when it's blessed and highly
> enchanted?

Do some googling and you'll find tables have been posted.  BUC
and luck both effect the rate so you want your luck maxed before
you start major shooting of arrows.  And that often means at least
after you come back up to minetown with the luckstone.



